I can't exactly pin down what this is meant to imply. It sounds tautological 
in English, but more so in Lojban. I read it as "A friend is going to be a 
friend.", which is why you should never ever ever ever ever translate words 
or phrases; you should translate meanings. Are you trying to state that one 
cannot prevent friends from being friends? If so, why not just say what you 
mean?

